        "name": "ESCALERA.ESPECIALMENTE.PROTEGIDA",
        "definition": "Staircase that meets the conditions of a protected staircase and also has a different independence vestibule at each of its accesses from each floor. The existence of said independence vestibule is not necessary when it is an open-air staircase, nor on the building's exit floor, when it is a staircase for ascending evacuation, and the staircase on said floor may lack compartmentalization.",
